From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: drm/exynos: mixer: use an overlay plane with fixed
 stacking order

The mixer on Exynos 5422 has no video processor, so it only has two
graphics layers. The second one is exposed as a cursor plane, which
Kodi does not use for direct-to-plane video rendering.

The mixer also only blends a graphics layer over the layers below it in
the default order (layer 1 over layer 0), as the vendor kernel assumes
("layer1 - OSD, layer0 - framebuffer"). With a mutable zpos, Kodi moves
layer 0 on top of layer 1 for its GUI, and the video below is hidden.

Expose layer 1 as an overlay plane and make the zpos of both graphics
layers immutable, so that Kodi puts the GUI on layer 1 and the video on
layer 0 without any Kodi change.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos_mixer.c
@@ -129,16 +129,14 @@
 		.pixel_formats = mixer_formats,
 		.num_pixel_formats = ARRAY_SIZE(mixer_formats),
 		.capabilities = EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_DOUBLE |
-				EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_ZPOS |
 				EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_PIX_BLEND |
 				EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_WIN_BLEND,
 	}, {
 		.zpos = 1,
-		.type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR,
+		.type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY,
 		.pixel_formats = mixer_formats,
 		.num_pixel_formats = ARRAY_SIZE(mixer_formats),
 		.capabilities = EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_DOUBLE |
-				EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_ZPOS |
 				EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_PIX_BLEND |
 				EXYNOS_DRM_PLANE_CAP_WIN_BLEND,
 	}, {
